## Implementation Order

1. **`strategies/base.py`** — define `BaseStrategy` ABC and `Signal` dataclass (BUY / SELL / HOLD, bar index, price). Nothing runs yet but the contract is set.

2. **`strategies/engulfing.py`** — implement `EngulfingStrategy(BaseStrategy)`:
   - `detect(prev, curr)` → `Signal` — pure function, easy to unit test
   - Bullish: prev is red (open > close), curr is green (close > open), curr engulfs prev body entirely
   - Bearish: opposite direction
   - No lookahead: only prev and curr bar are used

3. **`tests/test_engulfing.py`** — 8+ synthetic OHLCV rows covering:
   - Classic bullish engulf → BUY signal
   - Classic bearish engulf → SELL signal
   - Partial overlap (not engulfing) → HOLD
   - Doji candles (tiny bodies) → HOLD
   - Same-direction candles → HOLD
   All tests use hard-coded DataFrames; no network calls.

4. **`strategies/paper_engine.py`** — bar-by-bar replay engine:
   - Accepts any `BaseStrategy` instance + intraday DataFrame
   - Manages one open position at a time (flat → long or short → flat)
   - Configurable: `position_dollars`, `stop_loss_pct`, `take_profit_pct`
   - Closes position at end of session regardless (no overnight holds)
   - Returns per-trade log DataFrame and equity curve Series

5. **`tests/test_intraday_sim.py`** — engine tests with synthetic bar sequences:
   - Signal fires → position opens at next bar open
   - Stop-loss hit → position closes at stop price
   - Take-profit hit → closes at TP price
   - End-of-session force-close
   - Equity math correct (no lookahead into close price at signal bar)

6. **`intraday_sim.py`** — CLI wiring:
   - `--strategy engulfing` (default, extensible)
   - `--tickers` / `--tickers_file`
   - `--interval 5m` (default; also accepts `15m`, `30m`, `60m`)
   - `--start` / `--end` date range
   - `--position_dollars`, `--stop_loss_pct`, `--take_profit_pct`
   - `--out_csv` for equity curve, `--trades_csv` for trade log
   - Fetches data via `yfinance.download(..., interval=interval)` — no live feed needed

7. **`pyproject.toml`** — add `intraday-sim = "intraday_sim:main"` to `[project.scripts]`, add `intraday_sim` to `py-modules`.

8. **Verify full run** — `uv run intraday-sim --strategy engulfing --tickers AAPL --interval 5m --start 2026-04-01` produces a trades CSV and prints a metrics summary.

